spec:
  grid: (n_segs+1)–(2*n_segs+1) rows x (n_segs+1) cols, where n_segs is 2–7
  background: 0
  stripe:
    description: full-width solid row of color 8 on the bottom row
  segments:
    count: exactly w-1 (one per length 1..w-1)
    lengths: exactly {1, 2, ..., w-1}, all unique
    each_segment: single-row horizontal contiguous bar, one cell thick
    colors: each segment has a distinct non-0 non-8 color; all colors unique
    placement: scattered above the stripe, each on its own row, at arbitrary horizontal position
    row_gaps: adjacent segment rows separated by 1–2 rows [observed]
    no segment on the row directly above the stripe [observed]
  output:
    all segments cleared from original positions
    segments stacked in consecutive rows immediately above the stripe
    sorted by length shortest(top) to longest(bottom), right-aligned to grid edge
    stripe unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick n_segs in [2,7], set w = n_segs + 1
    2. Pick h in [n_segs+1, 2*n_segs+1] (must have h-1 >= n_segs rows above stripe)
    3. Assign n_segs distinct colors from {1..9}\{8} to lengths 1..w-1
    4. Build output grid (h x w) with bg=0, stripe row h-1 all 8, segments right-aligned sorted by length in rows (h-1-n_segs) .. (h-2)
    5. To get input, clear the stacked segments and scatter each to a random row above the stripe (each on a unique row), at a random horizontal offset that fits within width
    6. Validate no two segments share a row and all rows are above the stripe
